 "notes": "K-Rb-21Ne comagnetometer (ChangE) broadband axion DM search, 0.01-1000 Hz. Headline result: 95% CL limit on axion-neutron coupling g_ann [GeV^-1] (Fig. 4, gann_final.pdf from the e-print; the paper also bounds g_app but presents g_ann first/as headline). Paper convention: H = g_aNN grad(a).I with g_aNN = xi_n g_ann + xi_p g_app (xi_n^Ne=0.58/3); converted to canonical dimensionless g_an = 2 m_n x g_ann (2m_N rule for GeV^-1 gradient couplings), m_a = h f_a. Curve digitised from the vector figure: the paper's own 0.99fa-1.01fa binned 'guide-the-eye' curves - navy 'This work (SC)' for 0.01-3 Hz and brown 'This work (HSR)' for 6-1000 Hz - with the 3-6 Hz gap filled by the log-bin median of the raw (thin red) limit curve; the raw limit oscillates by factors of a few about this binned curve due to DM stochasticity. Cross-checks vs text: SC minimum 2.7e-10 GeV^-1 (paper: ~3e-10 in [0.02,4] Hz), HSR ~3e-9 GeV^-1 flat in [3,30] Hz then rising ~fa^2 (paper Materials & Methods). rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3. Full tabulated limits are only on an external GitHub repo cited by the paper (not consulted).",
